### Assumptions and Preconditions

- The wallet currently accepts an image hash whose configuration includes a nonzero checkpointer address.
- The checkpointer would report a newer snapshot or checkpoint that should make the stale configuration unusable.
- The attacker can produce sufficient signatures under the stale configuration, for example because old keys were compromised or a revoked signer set is still known.
