In `BaseSig.recover`, the checkpointer trust boundary is crossed before the signature is authenticated.

When the checkpointer flag bit (0x40) is set in the attacker-controlled `signatureFlag` read from the first byte of `_signature` using `_signature.readFirstUint8()`, the parser enters the checkpointer branch solely based on that flag (provided `_checkpointer == address(0)`). Immediately after, `_checkpointer` is read directly from `_signature` using `_signature.readAddress(rindex)`.

The code then reads an attacker-controlled 24-bit `checkpointerDataSize` using `_signature.readUint24(rindex)`, copies that many bytes from calldata into memory as `checkpointerData = _signature[rindex:rindex + checkpointerDataSize]`, and immediately performs an external call:

```solidity
